From bdb6f0420e797de9266de593326368091085cc3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mecattaf <thomas@leger.run>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 23:21:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] [ROCm] Apply the #52970 fp8 dot upcast to the
 block-scaled linear kernel

The MoE admission commit gives gfx1151 a working block-FP8 fused MoE,
but the dense projections were still broken:
TritonFp8BlockScaledMMKernel.is_supported admits every CUDA-alike
device, so the block-FP8 linear layers of this checkpoint dispatch to
_w8a8_triton_block_scaled_mm, which hands fp8 A/B tiles straight to
tl.dot -- unlowerable on RDNA3.5 (no FP8 WMMA) with Triton < 3.8.0.
The MoE would run and every dense projection would not.

Port the identical mechanism (vllm-project/vllm#52970) into the linear
kernel: a FORCE_FP8_DOT_UPCAST tl.constexpr (default False) that
converts the loaded tiles to bf16 before tl.dot, gated by
_w8a8_fp8_dot_upcast_on_gfx1151() -- ROCm + on_gfx1151() +
Triton < 3.8.0, mirroring the fused-MoE gate. The block-scale
multiplies stay in fp32, so numerics are the same block-scaled GEMM.
Logs once when engaged.

Kill switch: FN_FP8_LINEAR=0 (default on), the linear twin of
FN_FP8_MOE. Setting it restores the stock kernel byte-for-byte for
bisection.

Adds tests/kernels/quantization/test_gfx1151_fp8_linear_upcast.py: the
version gate, the kill switch, the gfx1151-only scope and the kernel
signature pin, all GPU-free.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01D273pHHi5ExDmStQUAicb7
